# Architecture

## Non-negotiables

- Preserve behavior while migrating. Do not combine large moves with behavior changes.
- `:androidApp` is a thin launcher/application module. Keep app logic in `:composeApp` or future feature/core modules.
- `:composeApp` is currently the migration host. New code should still follow package-level layer boundaries.
- `:shared` contains KMP-safe code. Do not add Android-only APIs to `commonMain`.
- Use `:build-logic` convention plugins for module defaults instead of repeating Gradle boilerplate.

## Target Module Shape

Use this target shape for new feature extraction:

```text
:core:domain
:core:data
:core:presentation
:core:design-system
:feature:<name>:domain
:feature:<name>:data
:feature:<name>:presentation
```

Dependency direction:

```text
presentation -> domain <- data
presentation -> core-presentation/core-design-system/core-domain
data -> core-data/core-domain
domain -> core-domain only
```

Features do not depend directly on other feature implementations. Cross-feature behavior goes through domain contracts, shared core APIs, or callbacks owned by the app navigation layer.

## Current Migration Rules

Because most functionality still lives in `composeApp/src/androidMain`, enforce the target layers by package:

- `domain/**`: pure contracts, models, use cases. No Compose, Android UI, Koin, Room, OkHttp, DataStore.
- `data/**`: repositories, prefs, API/local coordination. May implement domain contracts.
- `network/**`: network clients, DTO/network result handling.
- `ui/**` and `viewmodel/**`: presentation state, Compose screens, user actions.
- `navigation/**`: app graph assembly and cross-screen routing.
- `di/**`: Koin module assembly only.

When extracting a feature, first create the public domain contract, then move data and presentation in separate commits.

## DI

- Koin modules are composition roots. Prefer interface-to-implementation bindings.
- ViewModels are injected at screen/root boundaries.
- New feature DI belongs near the feature package/module and is included from app-level module assembly.
- Avoid service locator calls from UI and domain code.

## Verification

Run:

```bash
./gradlew productionArchitectureCheck
```

This enforces the thin launcher rule and prints current migration debt so future work can reduce it without breaking existing behavior.

